# Force LF line endings for text files, regardless of a contributor's
# core.autocrlf. Windows autocrlf was checking files out as CRLF, which broke
# \n-sensitive parsing (e.g. the notebook-import block regexes) and showed up as
# spurious churn. git auto-detects binary by content; the explicit entries below
# are belt-and-suspenders for known binary assets so eol normalization never
# touches them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.woff2  binary
*.woff   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.wasm   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.gcupkg binary
*.gcudat binary
